things built. Most of the macroscopic structures we will have them create
won't need perfect atom-resolution accuracy, but building the assemblers
themselves requires very high resolution positioning of atoms.

 The first generation nanites may require a super-mega-expensive
"cleanroom". Great vacuum, little vibration/contamination, and precise
atomic control.


